# Exception Handling Patterns

## Overview
The timesheet microservice uses a comprehensive exception handling strategy with custom exceptions, global exception handlers, and standardized error responses. This ensures consistent error handling across all layers of the application.

## Exception Hierarchy

### 1. Base Exception Classes
```java
// Base exception for all application exceptions
public abstract class TimesheetException extends RuntimeException {
    private final String errorCode;
    
    protected TimesheetException(String message, String errorCode) {
        super(message);
        this.errorCode = errorCode;
    }
    
    protected TimesheetException(String message, String errorCode, Throwable cause) {
        super(message, cause);
        this.errorCode = errorCode;
    }
    
    public String getErrorCode() {
        return errorCode;
    }
}
```

### 2. Custom Exception Types
```java
// Validation errors
public class ValidationErrorException extends TimesheetException {
    public ValidationErrorException(String message) {
        super(message, "VALIDATION_ERROR");
    }
    
    public ValidationErrorException(String message, Throwable cause) {
        super(message, "VALIDATION_ERROR", cause);
    }
}

// Resource not found errors
public class ResourceNotFoundException extends TimesheetException {
    public ResourceNotFoundException(String message) {
        super(message, "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND");
    }
    
    public ResourceNotFoundException(String resourceType, Object id) {
        super(String.format("%s not found with id: %s", resourceType, id), "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND");
    }
}

// Access control errors
public class UnauthorizedAccessException extends TimesheetException {
    public UnauthorizedAccessException(String message) {
        super(message, "UNAUTHORIZED_ACCESS");
    }
    
    public UnauthorizedAccessException(String message, Throwable cause) {
        super(message, "UNAUTHORIZED_ACCESS", cause);
    }
}

// Service layer errors
public class ServiceException extends TimesheetException {
